  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistance for the Bhutan Hydro and Solar Energy Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Project includes two components:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;(1) investments in both solar PV and mid-size run-of the river hydro (up to 75 MW or higher as agreed on a case-by-case basis) across Bhutan, to be co-financed by the Bank Loan (and thus representing the Bank Contribution to the Project) for up to 50% of total investment cost (on a portfolio basis).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;(2) the technical assistance, which constitutes the Action under this Contribution Agreement (and is further described in Annex 1(a) (&lt;em&gt;Operational Guidelines for the Technical Assistance Window A&lt;/em&gt;) and Annex&amp;nbsp;1(b)&amp;nbsp;(&lt;em&gt;Operational Guidelines for the Technical Assistance Window B&lt;/em&gt;) below).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Bank Loan and the corresponding Finance Contract, which benefit from the NDICI-Investment Window 1 guarantee, represents the EIB&#xbf;s first financing operation in Bhutan. The Sub-Projects to be supported thereunder are expected to generate positive economic impacts, deliver a strong climate contribution, and help Bhutan boost its energy security while diversifying its renewable energy mix.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;As a general approach, the due diligence for each allocation (&lt;em&gt;i.e.&lt;/em&gt;, Sub-Project) under the Bank Loan will be carried out by the Bank on a rolling basis during the availability period of the Bank Loan, as and when eligible Sub-Projects are presented to the Bank.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;In order to support the implementation of the Project, the Action, as further described in Annex&amp;nbsp;1(a)&amp;nbsp;(&lt;em&gt;Operational Guidelines for the Technical Assistance Window A&lt;/em&gt;) and Annex&amp;nbsp;1(b)&amp;nbsp;(&lt;em&gt;Operational Guidelines for the Technical Assistance Window B&lt;/em&gt;), is intended to support a number of green field renewable energy Sub-Projects that have so far been developed by Druk Green Power Corporation.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
